<title>GERMANY: Clarke-says G7 did not have in-depth talk on EMU.</title>
<headline>Clarke-says G7 did not have in-depth talk on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Saturday the Group of Seven (G7) nations did not discuss European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) in any substatial way.</p>
<p>At a news conference after the one-day meeting with his G7 counterparts, Clarke said the United States, Japan and Canada did not initiate any discussion about the euro, Europe's future single currency.</p>
</text>
